IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc11-definitions.l4 -- Part VIII.1 (Offences Relating to Conveyances), section 320.11 (Definitions), of the Criminal Code (Canada),
-- R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46. LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script,
-- of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified
-- against the official text. The French equivalents in parentheses after a defined term are quoted, not encoded.
-- Imports the keel's core only. A term the keel's section 2 defines (motor vehicle, railway equipment, peace officer, offender, bodily
-- harm) is taken as an INPUT named for its section (PLAN.md section 4 and 6); the keel's own functions answer it (ccc-definitions.l4).
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A caller never turns NOTHING into
-- FALSE. See NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc11)".
--
-- The lead-in of section 320.11 ("The following definitions apply in this Part.") is enacting words: inert (reason 1). It scopes every
-- definition below to Part VIII.1 (sections 320.11 to 320.4), which is why this part encodes them and the other parts ask for them as inputs.

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.11: the Kleene helpers used by the rules of this part`

-- Three small helpers (Kleene logic over a MAYBE BOOLEAN), so that a rule with an input that is "not covered" does not decide a case the text leaves open.
-- They are not provisions and carry no kind tag: a "no" they return is the "no" an operand already said, and the operand's own FALSE-kind stands behind it.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.11 helper: both hold` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS (JUST FALSE) OR b EQUALS (JUST FALSE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- helper: an operand said no
        IF a EQUALS (JUST TRUE) AND b EQUALS (JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- helper: an operand is not covered

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.11 helper: either holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS (JUST TRUE) OR b EQUALS (JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF a EQUALS (JUST FALSE) AND b EQUALS (JUST FALSE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- helper: both operands said no
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- helper: an operand is not covered

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.11 helper: the opposite of` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (NOT x)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- helper: an operand is not covered

-- Lines 6177-6181: the Part heading, the headings Interpretation and Definitions, and the lead-in of section 320.11: inert (reason 1, headings and enacting words).
-- src:6177 | PART VIII.1 Offences Relating to Conveyances
-- src:6179 | Interpretation
-- src:6180 | Definitions
-- src:6181 | 320.11 The following definitions apply in this Part.
§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.11: Definitions`

-- analyst means a person who is, or a person who is a member of a class of persons that is, designated by the Attorney General under subparagraph 320.4(b)(ii) or paragraph 320.4(c).
-- The designation itself is a fact (320.4 is the power to designate; it is encoded in ccc11-general.l4). Four facts: named or in a designated class, under (b)(ii) or under (c).
-- src:6182 | analyst means a person who is, or a person who is a member of a class of persons that is, designated by the Attorney General under subparagraph 320.4(b)(ii) or paragraph 320.4(c). (analyste)
@ref Criminal Code s 320.11 "analyst" (src:6182)
GIVEN `the person is designated by the Attorney General under subparagraph 320.4(b)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of a class of persons designated by the Attorney General under subparagraph 320.4(b)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is designated by the Attorney General under paragraph 320.4(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of a class of persons designated by the Attorney General under paragraph 320.4(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.11 the person is an analyst` MEANS
    IF `the person is designated by the Attorney General under subparagraph 320.4(b)(ii)`
       OR `the person is a member of a class of persons designated by the Attorney General under subparagraph 320.4(b)(ii)`
       OR `the person is designated by the Attorney General under paragraph 320.4(c)`
       OR `the person is a member of a class of persons designated by the Attorney General under paragraph 320.4(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "analyst means a person who is, or a person who is a member of a class of persons that is, designated by the Attorney General under subparagraph 320.4(b)(ii) or paragraph 320.4(c)"

-- src:6183 | approved container means a container that is designed to receive a sample of a person’s blood for analysis and that is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(d). (contenant approuvé)
@ref Criminal Code s 320.11 "approved container" (src:6183)
GIVEN `it is a container that is designed to receive a sample of a person’s blood for analysis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.11 the container is an approved container` MEANS
    IF `it is a container that is designed to receive a sample of a person’s blood for analysis` AND `it is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(d)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "approved container means a container that is designed to receive a sample of a person’s blood for analysis and that is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(d)"

-- src:6184 | approved drug screening equipment means equipment that is designed to ascertain the presence of a drug in a person’s body and that is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(b). (matériel de détection des drogues approuvé)
@ref Criminal Code s 320.11 "approved drug screening equipment" (src:6184)
GIVEN `it is equipment that is designed to ascertain the presence of a drug in a person’s body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.11 the equipment is approved drug screening equipment` MEANS
    IF `it is equipment that is designed to ascertain the presence of a drug in a person’s body` AND `it is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "approved drug screening equipment means equipment that is designed to ascertain the presence of a drug in a person’s body and that is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(b)"

-- src:6185 | approved instrument means an instrument that is designed to receive and make an analysis of a sample of a person’s breath to determine their blood alcohol concentration and that is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(c). (éthylomètre approuvé)
@ref Criminal Code s 320.11 "approved instrument" (src:6185)
GIVEN `it is an instrument that is designed to receive and make an analysis of a sample of a person’s breath to determine their blood alcohol concentration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.11 the instrument is an approved instrument` MEANS
    IF `it is an instrument that is designed to receive and make an analysis of a sample of a person’s breath to determine their blood alcohol concentration` AND `it is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "approved instrument means an instrument that is designed to receive and make an analysis of a sample of a person’s breath to determine their blood alcohol concentration and that is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(c)"

-- src:6186 | approved screening device means a device that is designed to ascertain the presence of alcohol in a person’s blood and that is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(a). (appareil de détection approuvé)
@ref Criminal Code s 320.11 "approved screening device" (src:6186)
GIVEN `it is a device that is designed to ascertain the presence of alcohol in a person’s blood` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.11 the device is an approved screening device` MEANS
    IF `it is a device that is designed to ascertain the presence of alcohol in a person’s blood` AND `it is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "approved screening device means a device that is designed to ascertain the presence of alcohol in a person’s blood and that is approved by the Attorney General of Canada under paragraph 320.39(a)"

-- vessel includes a hovercraft. "Vessel" is not otherwise defined in the Act, so the ordinary sense is asked as a fact (a borrowed term); a thing that is
-- neither a hovercraft nor a vessel in that sense is NOT COVERED (the definition "includes"; it does not close the term), never "not a vessel".
-- src:6197 | vessel includes a hovercraft. (bateau)
@ref Criminal Code s 320.11 "vessel" (src:6197)
GIVEN `it is a hovercraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a vessel in the ordinary sense of the word` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.11 the thing is a vessel` MEANS
    IF `it is a hovercraft` OR `it is a vessel in the ordinary sense of the word`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "vessel includes a hovercraft"

-- conveyance means a motor vehicle, a vessel, an aircraft or railway equipment. "Aircraft" is not defined in the Act: asked as a fact.
-- A caller who has an answer for the section 2 terms passes it; a NOTHING among them that no other limb overrides gives NOTHING.
-- src:6187 | conveyance means a motor vehicle, a vessel, an aircraft or railway equipment. (moyen de transport)
@ref Criminal Code s 320.11 "conveyance" (src:6187)
GIVEN `it is a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is a vessel, by s 320.11 the thing is a vessel` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is an aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is railway equipment, by s 2 railway equipment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.11 the thing is a conveyance` MEANS
    `s 320.11 helper: either holds`
        (`s 320.11 helper: either holds` `it is a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` `it is a vessel, by s 320.11 the thing is a vessel`)
        (`s 320.11 helper: either holds` (JUST `it is an aircraft`) `it is railway equipment, by s 2 railway equipment`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "conveyance means a motor vehicle, a vessel, an aircraft or railway equipment"
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

-- src:6188 | evaluating officer means a peace officer who has the qualifications prescribed by regulation that are required in order to act as an evaluating officer. (agent évaluateur)
@ref Criminal Code s 320.11 "evaluating officer" (src:6188)
GIVEN `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has the qualifications prescribed by regulation (paragraph 320.38(a)) that are required in order to act as an evaluating officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.11 the person is an evaluating officer` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person has the qualifications prescribed by regulation (paragraph 320.38(a)) that are required in order to act as an evaluating officer`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "evaluating officer means a peace officer who has the qualifications prescribed by regulation that are required in order to act as an evaluating officer"
    ELSE `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE or NOTHING as s 2 "peace officer" answers ("includes": NOTHING for a capacity the list does not name)

-- operate means (a) motor vehicle: drive it or have care or control of it; (b) vessel or aircraft: navigate it, assist in its navigation or have care or control of it;
-- (c) railway equipment: participate in the direct control of its motion, or have care or control of it as a member of the equipment's crew, as a person who acts in lieu of a member
-- of the equipment's crew by remote control, or otherwise. Reading taken for (c): "or otherwise" makes care or control in ANY capacity enough (fork, NOTES.md).
-- The "no" of this function is the "means" of the definition: it is JUST FALSE when every limb that could apply says no.
-- src:6189 | operate means
-- src:6190 | (a) in respect of a motor vehicle, to drive it or to have care or control of it;
-- src:6191 | (b) in respect of a vessel or aircraft, to navigate it, to assist in its navigation or to have care or control of it; and
-- src:6192 | (c) in respect of railway equipment, to participate in the direct control of its motion, or to have care or control of it as a member of the equipment’s crew, as a person who acts in lieu of a member of the equipment’s crew by remote control, or otherwise. (conduire)
@ref Criminal Code s 320.11 "operate" (src:6189-6192)
GIVEN `it is a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is a vessel, by s 320.11 the thing is a vessel` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is an aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is railway equipment, by s 2 railway equipment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person drove it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person navigated it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person assisted in its navigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person participated in the direct control of its motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had care or control of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "operate means (a) in respect of a motor vehicle, to drive it or to have care or control of it"
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in respect of a vessel or aircraft, to navigate it, to assist in its navigation or to have care or control of it"
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) in respect of railway equipment, to participate in the direct control of its motion"
    `s 320.11 helper: either holds` (`s 320.11 helper: either holds` limbA limbB) limbC
    WHERE
        limbA MEANS `s 320.11 helper: both hold` `it is a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` (JUST (`the person drove it` OR `the person had care or control of it`))
        limbB MEANS `s 320.11 helper: both hold` (`s 320.11 helper: either holds` `it is a vessel, by s 320.11 the thing is a vessel` (JUST `it is an aircraft`)) (JUST (`the person navigated it` OR `the person assisted in its navigation` OR `the person had care or control of it`))
        limbC MEANS `s 320.11 helper: both hold` `it is railway equipment, by s 2 railway equipment` (JUST (`the person participated in the direct control of its motion` OR `the person had care or control of it`))
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

-- src:6193 | qualified medical practitioner means a person who is qualified under provincial law to practise medicine. (médecin qualifié)
@ref Criminal Code s 320.11 "qualified medical practitioner" (src:6193)
GIVEN `the person is qualified under provincial law to practise medicine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` MEANS
    IF `the person is qualified under provincial law to practise medicine`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "qualified medical practitioner means a person who is qualified under provincial law to practise medicine"

-- qualified technician means (a) in respect of breath samples, a person designated by the Attorney General under paragraph 320.4(a); and (b) in respect of blood samples,
-- a person who is, or is a member of a class of persons that is, designated by the Attorney General under subparagraph 320.4(b)(i). Two functions, one per limb: the limb that applies
-- is the one for the kind of sample.
-- src:6194 | qualified technician means
-- src:6195 | (a) in respect of breath samples, a person who is designated by the Attorney General under paragraph 320.4(a); and
@ref Criminal Code s 320.11 "qualified technician" (a) (src:6194-6195)
GIVEN `the person is designated by the Attorney General under paragraph 320.4(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples` MEANS
    IF `the person is designated by the Attorney General under paragraph 320.4(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "qualified technician means (a) in respect of breath samples, a person who is designated by the Attorney General under paragraph 320.4(a)"

-- src:6196 | (b) in respect of blood samples, a person who is, or a person who is a member of a class of persons that is, designated by the Attorney General under subparagraph 320.4(b)(i). (technicien qualifié)
@ref Criminal Code s 320.11 "qualified technician" (b) (src:6196)
GIVEN `the person is designated by the Attorney General under subparagraph 320.4(b)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of a class of persons designated by the Attorney General under subparagraph 320.4(b)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples` MEANS
    IF `the person is designated by the Attorney General under subparagraph 320.4(b)(i)` OR `the person is a member of a class of persons designated by the Attorney General under subparagraph 320.4(b)(i)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in respect of blood samples, a person who is, or a person who is a member of a class of persons that is, designated by the Attorney General under subparagraph 320.4(b)(i)"

-- Section 320.12 (Recognition and declaration, lines 6199-6205) is "It is recognized and declared that (a) ... (d) ...": a declaration of policy and of the reliability of two
-- methods. It creates no rule and no relation: inert (reason 1, a purpose clause). Quoted here so the locators cover it.
-- src:6199 | Recognition and Declaration
-- src:6200 | Recognition and declaration
-- src:6201 | 320.12 It is recognized and declared that
-- src:6202 | (a) operating a conveyance is a privilege that is subject to certain limits in the interests of public safety that include licensing, the observance of rules and sobriety;
-- src:6203 | (b) the protection of society is well served by deterring persons from operating conveyances dangerously or while their ability to operate them is impaired by alcohol or a drug, because that conduct poses a threat to the life, health and safety of Canadians;
-- src:6204 | (c) the analysis of a sample of a person’s breath by means of an approved instrument produces reliable and accurate readings of blood alcohol concentration; and
-- src:6205 | (d) an evaluation conducted by an evaluating officer is a reliable method of determining whether a person’s ability to operate a conveyance is impaired by a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug.
